{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017thRzguRKceVSxhGJerscc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translated from c_src/src/lib.c.\n2\t//! All routines preserve the exact semantics of the C originals (including\n3\t//! quirks). The buffer in the executable is bounded to 256 elements and\n4\t//! operations only shrink or preserve length, so the public function operates\n5\t//! on a slice in-place and returns the new logical length.\n6\t\n7\t/// Main entrance function - processes buffer based on operation flags.\n8\t///\n9\t/// Bit flags:\n10\t///   bit 0: rotate buffer\n11\t///   bit 1: compact runs\n12\t///   bit 2: remove duplicates\n13\t///   bit 3: interleave halves\n14\t///   bit 4: reverse segments\n15\tpub fn process_buffer(\n16\t    buffer: &mut [u8],\n17\t    length: usize,\n18\t    flags: u32,\n19\t    param1: i32,\n20\t    param2: i32,\n21\t) -> usize {\n22\t    let mut new_len = length;\n23\t\n24\t    if buffer.is_empty() || length == 0 {\n25\t        return 0;\n26\t    }\n27\t\n28\t    // Rotate\n29\t    if flags & 0x01 != 0 {\n30\t        let offset = param1.rem_euclid_c(length as i32);\n31\t        // C does `param1 % (int)length` (truncated toward zero).\n32\t        // We replicate that truncated remainder here, not Rust's rem_euclid.\n33\t        let offset = (param1 as i64 % length as i64) as i32;\n34\t        if offset != 0 {\n35\t            rotate_buffer(buffer, length, offset);\n36\t        }\n37\t        let _ = offset; // silence unused warning if any\n38\t    }\n39\t\n40\t    // Compact runs\n41\t    if flags & 0x02 != 0 {\n42\t        let threshold: u8 = if param1 > 0 && param1 <= 255 {\n43\t            param1 as u8\n44\t        } else {\n45\t            3\n46\t        };\n47\t        new_len = compact_runs(buffer, new_len, threshold);\n48\t    }\n49\t\n50\t    // Remove duplicates\n51\t    if flags & 0x04 != 0 {\n52\t        let preserve = param2 != 0;\n53\t        new_len = remove_duplicates(bu